usage: stub [-h] [--version] [--json PATH] [--tallies] [--secret] [--one]
            [--two]

A stub subject the harness's own --selftest drives. It prints a report
carrying its working directory and the microseconds the scan took, writes a
JSON export with a provenance block, prints a fenced tally block, and refuses
one flag combination. This description is long enough that argparse has to
wrap it at the terminal width, which is what the census's COLUMNS pin is for.

options:
  -h, --help   show this help message and exit
  --version    print the stub's version and exit, and nothing else at all
  --json PATH  write the export to PATH; the provenance block carries the
               commit this tree is at
  --tallies    print the fenced group blocks a tallies surface reduces to one
               verdict line each
  --secret     print the constant no recorded surface carries
  --one        the first half of the combination that composes with nothing
  --two        the second half; naming both is the refusal
